{
  "source": "Prompts/vector-space-5.mp4",
  "duration": 213.1824375,
  "segments": [
    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 3.96,
      "text": "Each token starts with a row of numbers, called an embedding."
    },
    {
      "start": 4.48,
      "end": 10.08,
      "text": "As an AI processes your message, the layers constantly change those numbers to reflect the context."
    },
    {
      "start": 10.78,
      "end": 14.32,
      "text": "But those new numbers might not match the starting numbers for any token."
    },
    {
      "start": 14.92,
      "end": 16.28,
      "text": "How can they still represent meaning?"
    },
    {
      "start": 17.18,
      "end": 19.0,
      "text": "An exact match isn't necessary."
    },
    {
      "start": 19.62,
      "end": 21.9,
      "text": "The relationships between the numbers matter, too."
    },
    {
      "start": 22.8,
      "end": 28.76,
      "text": "We can picture those relationships as positions on a map, where nearby positions can represent similar meanings."
    },
    {
      "start": 28.76,
      "end": 31.52,
      "text": "That's the idea behind vector space."
    },
    {
      "start": 32.3,
      "end": 37.52,
      "text": "The system defines meaning as a relative position within a space, determined entirely by its neighbors."
    },
    {
      "start": 38.74,
      "end": 43.16,
      "text": "A standard map uses two numbers for a position, latitude and longitude."
    },
    {
      "start": 44.1,
      "end": 49.96,
      "text": "Let's add Dallas to the map at 32.78 degrees north, 96.80 degrees west."
    },
    {
      "start": 50.84,
      "end": 54.6,
      "text": "Next, add Mountain View at 37 north, 122 west."
    },
    {
      "start": 54.6,
      "end": 58.82,
      "text": "Then, plot New York City at 41 north, 74 west."
    },
    {
      "start": 59.82,
      "end": 64.64,
      "text": "Two specific numbers give us everything needed to perfectly define a fixed location on a map."
    },
    {
      "start": 65.58,
      "end": 70.96,
      "text": "Now, suppose you receive new coordinates. 38 degrees north, 120 degrees west."
    },
    {
      "start": 71.7,
      "end": 73.64,
      "text": "Let's mark this unknown position with a diamond."
    },
    {
      "start": 74.52,
      "end": 76.8,
      "text": "Which of our three established cities is closest?"
    },
    {
      "start": 78.02,
      "end": 79.0,
      "text": "Mountain View is closest."
    },
    {
      "start": 79.0,
      "end": 84.58,
      "text": "The coordinates do not match exactly, but calculating distance easily identifies the nearest city."
    },
    {
      "start": 85.66,
      "end": 90.06,
      "text": "Let's try a second unknown position at 40 degrees north, 76 degrees west."
    },
    {
      "start": 90.98,
      "end": 93.84,
      "text": "Looking at this second diamond, which city is closest now?"
    },
    {
      "start": 94.94,
      "end": 96.32,
      "text": "New York City is the closest match."
    },
    {
      "start": 97.84,
      "end": 100.68,
      "text": "Distance measurements overcome the lack of an exact coordinate match."
    },
    {
      "start": 101.48,
      "end": 107.56,
      "text": "Calculating the distance between points allows the system to find the closest match, even when the raw data is imprecise."
    },
    {
      "start": 108.34,
      "end": 111.46,
      "text": "This diagram maps drinks on seven flavor characteristics."
    },
    {
      "start": 112.5,
      "end": 115.1,
      "text": "Let's start with Coke's seven numbers for sweetness and fizz."
    },
    {
      "start": 115.98,
      "end": 120.44,
      "text": "Pepsi's numbers are nearly identical, so it plots right next to it in a soft drinks neighborhood."
    },
    {
      "start": 121.44,
      "end": 126.04,
      "text": "Hot coffee scores differ significantly, plotting far away in a coffee and tea neighborhood."
    },
    {
      "start": 127.1,
      "end": 130.16,
      "text": "Expanding from two coordinates to seven does not change the rules."
    },
    {
      "start": 130.76,
      "end": 135.44,
      "text": "It simply creates more dimensions to map exactly how similar or different objects are."
    },
    {
      "start": 135.44,
      "end": 137.88,
      "text": "Let's introduce Mystery Drink A."
    },
    {
      "start": 138.52,
      "end": 140.88,
      "text": "Its first six numbers match the sodas perfectly."
    },
    {
      "start": 141.52,
      "end": 143.06,
      "text": "We compare the seventh number, citrus."
    },
    {
      "start": 144.08,
      "end": 145.48,
      "text": "Pepsi is the closest match."
    },
    {
      "start": 146.1,
      "end": 148.18,
      "text": "Mystery Drink A's citrus score is 9."
    },
    {
      "start": 148.72,
      "end": 152.44,
      "text": "The mathematical gap to Pepsi's 10 is much smaller than Coke's 1."
    },
    {
      "start": 153.1,
      "end": 155.04,
      "text": "Now let's plot Mystery Drink B."
    },
    {
      "start": 155.8,
      "end": 158.66,
      "text": "Compare all seven of its numbers against our established drinks."
    },
    {
      "start": 159.22,
      "end": 160.38,
      "text": "Which one is the closest neighbor?"
    },
    {
      "start": 161.22,
      "end": 162.64,
      "text": "Hot coffee is the match."
    },
    {
      "start": 162.64,
      "end": 166.06,
      "text": "The numerical ratings are similar across all seven dimensions."
    },
    {
      "start": 166.78,
      "end": 170.1,
      "text": "Comparing numbers across multiple dimensions finds the closest match."
    },
    {
      "start": 170.88,
      "end": 173.9,
      "text": "Smaller numerical gaps always mean closer spatial positions."
    },
    {
      "start": 174.82,
      "end": 178.9,
      "text": "Real AI scales this logic up, using thousands of dimensions to represent meaning."
    },
    {
      "start": 179.8,
      "end": 183.78,
      "text": "Let's trace how context shifts a word's position using a specific sentence."
    },
    {
      "start": 184.42,
      "end": 188.14,
      "text": "The cat sat on the mat during the May rainstorm because it was tired."
    },
    {
      "start": 188.14,
      "end": 193.52,
      "text": "On its own, the ambiguous token IT starts resting at specific numerical coordinates."
    },
    {
      "start": 194.28,
      "end": 198.82,
      "text": "As AI layers process the sentence, they actively update the numbers for IT,"
    },
    {
      "start": 199.22,
      "end": 201.42,
      "text": "forcing it to physically move through vector space."
    },
    {
      "start": 202.12,
      "end": 204.62,
      "text": "Its new position reflects its connection to cat."
    },
    {
      "start": 205.46,
      "end": 207.22,
      "text": "Meaning is a position in vector space."
    },
    {
      "start": 208.08,
      "end": 209.64,
      "text": "Similar meanings usually sit close together."
    }
  ],
